{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug repair amendment. Problem: the first full-suite run after adding five-second isolation probes completed 13,720 tests but produced three teardown errors. Proven cause: tests monkeypatched the shared subprocess module's run attribute; the autouse repo guard dereferenced that mutable attribute before pytest restored it, so its own HEAD probe invoked each test-local timeout fake. Focused runtime RED: the three exact nodes passed their call phase but errored at teardown (3 passed, 3 errors). Fix: tests/_isolation.py now binds the real process runner at import and both HEAD/status probes use that stable boundary while retaining timeout=5. Held-out GREEN: the untouched three nodes pass in 0.61s. Exact-defect mutation changed both calls back to subprocess.run and restored precisely 3 teardown errors; restoring the binding returned them green. Real blocked-Git negative controls plus the complete repo-isolation guard matrix pass (14 passed in 13.81s), proving genuine probe hangs still raise TimeoutExpired within the five-second watchdog. Lint, complexity, formatting, diff check, and mypy (555 files) pass. Scope/safety: test infrastructure only, no dependency or production capability; no test weakened. Original hang scenario remains bounded, and subprocess timeout doubles no longer contaminate teardown. Full default-suite acceptance remains intentionally pending Gerrit Verified."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787078605730629001,"uuid":"d268031d-8c91-4a50-ae56-d6449bd0e90e"}